# Check every text file out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows with the default `core.autocrlf=true` gets a
# CRLF working tree while the committed content is LF — and biome's formatter
# defaults to `lineEnding: "lf"`, so `bunx biome check` reports **every file**
# as unformatted. 319 of them, on a tree that is byte-identical to one the same
# command called clean.
#
# It stayed invisible for the whole build because files edited in place keep the
# LF the editor wrote; only a fresh checkout re-runs the filter. It surfaced the
# first time the history was replayed, which is the first time this repo had
# been checked out rather than edited.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect and leave binaries alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
